<ProblemTable ticket={4471} only="one-day" what={{ 'one-day': 'The date moves by one day, no swap.' }} />

## What happened

No day and month swap: the date moves by one day.

> Invite says Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says Monday 11 May.
>
> Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday. Same meeting.
>
> Every booking in June is one day off. Only June.
>
> The invite arrived before I made the booking.
>
> Tuesday 6 October showed as Monday.

It looks like a time zone or DST conversion between the tenant, the attendee and UTC. The desk
read these as one-day moves (`desk-notes.json`), and the kb still files them under `parser` by
tenant, so they are counted there as well.

## How to recognise it

A date one day off, not swapped, from any tenant. The latest reporter (4 October) says they have
stopped reporting these, so the count is low.

## State

Open. Needs investigation of how invite dates are converted between time zones.

